import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Retro — _MAX_BINDING_ENVS: the composite gauntlet terminates, honestly","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — `_MAX_BINDING_ENVS`: the composite gauntlet terminates, honestly","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/binding-env-cap.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/binding-env-cap.md"}'),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/binding-env-cap.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-max-binding-envs-the-composite-gauntlet-terminates-honestly" tabindex="-1">Retro — <code>_MAX_BINDING_ENVS</code>: the composite gauntlet terminates, honestly <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-max-binding-envs-the-composite-gauntlet-terminates-honestly" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — _MAX_BINDING_ENVS: the composite gauntlet terminates, honestly”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Follows</strong>: <code>enablement-floor.md</code> (its named scaling gap: &quot;<code>run_gauntlet</code>/<code>pl.measure</code> on guarded minted composites does not terminate within the box&quot;) and <code>fold-cost-single-source.md</code>. <strong>Commit</strong>: this commit (<code>oracle._MAX_BINDING_ENVS</code>, the probe&#39;s gauntlet leg, two pins in <code>test_discovery_oracle.py</code>).</p><h2 id="the-hotspot-corrected" tabindex="-1">The hotspot, corrected <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-hotspot-corrected" aria-label="Permalink to “The hotspot, corrected”">​</a></h2><p>The retro named the 83-rule <code>_reach</code>/derivability saturation. Measured (<code>faulthandler</code> stacks + per-stage timers on the stored conv+BN composite, one-case corpus):</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>stage</th><th>measured</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>verify_law</code> (derivability, 83 rules)</td><td><strong>0.0 s</strong> — 54 enodes, not derivable</td></tr><tr><td><code>_probe</code> / <code>_typed_probe</code> (lone rule)</td><td>0.0 s each — 29 enodes</td></tr><tr><td><code>_reach</code> (<code>_saturate</code> ×2, 83/84 rules, budgeted)</td><td><strong>0.0 s</strong> — 9→54 enodes, <code>fixed_point</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>sweep_real</code></td><td>0.0 s — one real match</td></tr><tr><td><strong><code>oracle.synthesize</code></strong> (<code>verify_view_candidate</code>)</td><td><strong>never returned</strong> — the whole hang</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The explosion is not the e-graph; it is the <strong>binding-env enumeration</strong>. <code>synthesize</code>, <code>evidence._synth_sites</code> and <code>object_synthesis._oracle_sites</code> all cap the <em>sites they yield</em> — but a <code>derive</code> veto or an uninstantiable pair consumes an env without producing a site. The composite is a 4-deep <code>syn_*</code> composition whose composed <code>derive</code> declined <strong>2000/2000</strong> enumerated envs at ~8k envs/s on a domain orders past 10⁹ envs — every cap the consumers held was on the output side of a faucet that never dripped. This is the same failure class <code>_MAX_VIEWED_BINDINGS</code> closed one level down; the missing bound was on the env stream itself.</p><h2 id="the-fix" tabindex="-1">The fix <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-fix" aria-label="Permalink to “The fix”">​</a></h2><p><code>oracle._binding_envs</code> now stops after <code>_MAX_BINDING_ENVS = 250_000</code> yielded envs — a property of the enumeration machinery, so every consumer (<code>synthesize</code>, <code>_synth_sites</code>, <code>_oracle_sites</code>) inherits the bound unchanged. Sizing is measured, not guessed: the largest legitimate sweep observed is <code>sdpa_fold_nomask</code>&#39;s at ~180k envs to natural exhaustion under <code>synthesize</code> (its <code>derive</code> vetoes ~2 200:1 — the shipped worst case), so 250k preserves every shipped sweep with headroom while bounding a veto-everything domain to a fixed corner of the Cantor order — a partial sweep, the same honesty the instance and viewed-binding caps already document. (<code>rms_norm_fold</code>&#39;s leaf-only sweep measures 13.9M envs/134 s to exhaustion — it has no viewish op, so <code>synthesize</code> is unreachable for it through <code>measure</code>; the cap now bounds it too if it is ever swept directly.)</p><h2 id="the-measured-verdict" tabindex="-1">The measured verdict <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-measured-verdict" aria-label="Permalink to “The measured verdict”">​</a></h2><p><code>conv_fold_premise_pay_probe.py</code> now runs <code>run_gauntlet</code> end to end on the one-case corpus: <strong>4.9 s</strong> (was: &gt;9 min, unbounded). Stages: reconstruct ✓, full-data ✓ (guard transport), measure ✓, <strong>truth FAIL</strong> — <code>numeric=True</code>, <code>view=true</code> (the one evaluable instance agrees), but the guarded synth region is starved (<code>0 accepted / 2000 declined / 2360 envs</code>, escalation included) and <code>derivable=False</code> under <code>corpus.base_rules</code> (<code>ALL_RULES</code> — the premise closure is not in the search set). The refusal is the honest <em>starvation</em> verdict the gate documents: the enumeration bank cannot mint the conv-channel corner — the same &quot;corner-reaching truth route&quot; already named open — not a wrong answer and not a hang.</p><p><strong>Pay leg (unchanged, now confirmed under the gauntlet&#39;s own measure)</strong>: <code>fires=1 changed=True verified=pass</code>, <code>dag_cost</code> fused <code>17 438.7</code> vs spelled <code>34 874.3</code> — the FOLD_OPS single-sourcing made the composite a payer.</p><h2 id="what-stays-open" tabindex="-1">What stays open <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The truth gate&#39;s synth-side starvation for stored composites: the binding banks have no conv-weight-shaped inhabitants. The named fix remains a corner-reaching enumeration vocabulary (or witness-driven sites) — the cap bounds the <em>work</em>, it does not move the corner.</li><li>A stored composite&#39;s premises are outside <code>corpus.base_rules</code>, so <code>derivable</code> reads <code>False</code> where the premise-anchored replay (<code>verify_law</code> under <code>ALL_RULES + closure</code>) proves it. Whether the gauntlet corpus should carry the record&#39;s premise closure is a policy question, not a bound.</li></ul><p>Gate account: <code>tests/test_discovery_oracle.py</code> (+2 env-cap pins), <code>test_law_view_oracle.py</code>, <code>test_discovery_{gauntlet,evidence,pipeline, autocond,dspec_synth,synthesis,arena,meta_arena,enumerate,climb_b}</code>, <code>test_machine_pack.py</code>, <code>test_construction_gaps.py</code>, <code>test_conv_fold_rules.py</code>, <code>test_batch_norm_expand.py</code>, <code>test_guard_sweep.py</code> — all green (the one failure, <code>test_every_conditional_rule_is_swept</code> 125≠124, is pre-existing at <code>bb6a2c4</code> — verified with the fix stashed). ruff/format/ty clean on touched files.</p>`,14)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};